+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up and the account settings page (`/account`) support passkeys (WebAuthn) via [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/):
+
+- **Sign in** with a passkey button or via autofill on the username field (conditional UI). After a password sign-in, supporting browsers may silently offer to create a passkey (conditional create).
+- **Sign up** with a passkey only (no password), or with a password and an optional "create a passkey" step afterwards.
+- **Manage** passkeys in account settings: create, rename, and remove. Changes are reported to the passkey provider via the WebAuthn Signal API.
+- **Re-authentication**: adding or removing a passkey more than 5 minutes after signing in requires confirming with a passkey or password.
+
+Passwords are still verified by the external Times API, but those requests now go through this app's server so it can set up a session. Passkeys and local account records are stored in `.data/passkeys.json`.
