@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# Privacy by Design: The Daily Grind website
+
+This file records how the site handles personal data. It is the source of
+truth for the "Your privacy on this page" dialog in `index.html`. Update it,
+and get a privacy review, **before** you add any new data collection or third
+party.
+
+## Principles
+
+1. **Private by default.** No optional processing (analytics, marketing,
+   personalization) runs unless a user opts in. `window.DailyGrindPrivacy.allows()`
+   currently returns `false` for every purpose.
+2. **Data minimization.** Collect only what the current task needs. The
+   homepage collects nothing beyond the request itself.
+3. **No privacy labor.** We have nothing to consent to, so there is no consent
+   banner. A short transparency notice explains what happens instead.
+4. **Honor signals.** Global Privacy Control (`Sec-GPC: 1` /
+   `navigator.globalPrivacyControl`) counts as an opt-out of sale or sharing,
+   declared in `/.well-known/gpc.json`.
+
+## Data inventory (homepage)
+
+| Data | Where | Purpose | Retention | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Session cookie (signed-in users only) | `__Host-session`, set by the app server | Authentication | Until logout or expiry | `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax`. Cleared by `Clear-Site-Data` on logout |
+| Server access logs | Hosting provider | Security and abuse prevention | 30 days | Truncate IPs. Strip query strings, or run them through the same PII list as `js/privacy.js` |
+| CSP and Reporting API reports | `/api/security-reports` | Detect XSS and unexpected third parties | 30 days | Store the blocked origin only. Drop full URLs, `sample`, and cookies |
+| Web Storage | None | n/a | n/a | `js/privacy.js` clears it on logout anyway |
+
+> **TODO (owners: Legal/Ops):** confirm the retention periods and IP truncation
+> above match production. The transparency dialog makes these claims to users.
+
+## Third-party audit
+
+Last audit: **2026-11-22**. Method: reviewed the source plus CSP/resource
+timing. Repeat with a DevTools HAR capture on each release.
+
+| Third party | Previously used for | Data exposed | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `images.unsplash.com` | Hero background image, hot-linked from CSS | Visitor IP, user agent, Referer (page URL) on every homepage view | **Removed.** Image is now self-hosted via `npm run fetch-assets` |
+| (none) | Fonts | n/a | System font stack only, no web-font CDN |
+| (none) | Analytics, ads, social SDKs | n/a | None present |
+
+Outbound links (e.g. `globalprivacycontrol.org`) use
+`rel="noopener noreferrer"` and only load when the user clicks them.
+
+### Adding a third party (checklist)
+
+- [ ] Is it strictly necessary? Could we self-host it or build it first-party?
+- [ ] What data does it receive (IP, UA, cookies, page URL, user IDs)? Check a HAR capture.
+- [ ] Is there a privacy-preserving mode (e.g. `youtube-nocookie.com`, a click-to-load façade)?
+- [ ] Gate it behind `DailyGrindPrivacy.allows(purpose)` and user opt-in. Never load it when GPC is on, if it counts as sale or sharing.
+- [ ] Use a versioned URL with `integrity` + `crossorigin="anonymous"` + `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`.
+- [ ] Add the origin to the *narrowest* CSP directive in **both** `_headers` and the `<meta>` CSP, and to `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in `js/privacy.js`.
+- [ ] Update this file and the transparency dialog copy.
+
+## Technical controls
+
+| Control | Location |
+| --- | --- |
+| Strict CSP (`default-src 'none'`, no inline code, `connect-src 'none'`, Trusted Types, `frame-ancestors 'none'`) | `_headers`, `package.json` `start` (statikk `--csp`), `<meta>` in `index.html` |
+| `Referrer-Policy: same-origin` | `_headers`, `<meta name="referrer">` |
+| `Permissions-Policy` denying sensors, camera, mic, geolocation, Topics, etc. | `_headers` |
+| HSTS, `nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options`, COOP, CORP | `_headers` |
+| `Connection-Allowlist-Report-Only` (experimental; audits all outbound connections) | `_headers` |
+| Logout via POST + `Clear-Site-Data` + client storage clear | `index.html`, `js/privacy.js`, app server (see `_headers` notes) |
+| Strip PII, tokens and tracking click IDs from the URL | `js/privacy.js` (`scrubUrl`) |
+| Runtime third-party watchdog (console only, origin-only logging) | `js/privacy.js` (`setUpThirdPartyAudit`) |
+| No `Cache-Control: public` on HTML | `_headers` |
+
+## Server-side requirements (not in this repo)
+
+- `POST /logout`: CSRF token or `Sec-Fetch-Site` check, invalidate the session, respond with `Clear-Site-Data: "cookies", "storage", "cache"`.
+- `POST /api/security-reports`: accept `application/reports+json`, rate-limit it, and keep only `effectiveDirective` and the blocked **origin**.
+- Rate-limit account and profile endpoints to prevent scraping.
+- Data-subject requests (access, correction, deletion) self-serve at `/account/privacy`.
