@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+This document records how the seven privacy-by-design principles are applied
+to the public website, what data the site touches, and how third parties are
+reviewed. Run `pnpm audit:privacy` to verify the rules below automatically.
+
+## Layout
+
+| Path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `public/` | The **only** directory that is served. Source, docs and config are never exposed. |
+| `public/index.html` | Markup. No inline scripts, styles or event handlers. |
+| `public/assets/css/main.css` | All styles (system fonts only). |
+| `public/assets/js/privacy.js` | Consent/GPC handling, tracking-parameter stripping, identifier purge. |
+| `public/.well-known/gpc.json` | Declares Global Privacy Control support. |
+| `public/.well-known/security.txt` | Vulnerability-reporting contact (RFC 9116). |
+| `privacy/third-parties.json` | Third-party registry — single source of truth for allowed origins. |
+| `privacy/security-headers.mjs` | Builds CSP (from the registry) and all other response headers. |
+| `server.mjs` | Static server applying the headers (`pnpm start`, `pnpm start:prod`). |
+| `scripts/audit-privacy.mjs` | Automated privacy / third-party audit (`pnpm audit:privacy`). |
+
+## Data inventory (homepage)
+
+| Data | Collected? | Where | Retention |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Analytics / advertising identifiers | **No** | — | Any found are deleted on load unless consented. |
+| Privacy choice | Only when the visitor saves choices | `localStorage["dg.privacy.v1"]`, this device only | 180 days, then re-asked. Contains booleans + a date (no time, no ID). |
+| Session cookie | Set by the backend for sign-in (not by this page) | First-party cookie | Ended by `POST /logout`. Must be `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax`. |
+| IP / User-Agent | Inherent to HTTP | Our server; the Unsplash CDN for the hero image | Server log retention per privacy policy. |
+| Campaign parameters (`utm_*`, `gclid`, `fbclid`…) | **Stripped** from the URL on load | — | Not kept in history, bookmarks, or shared links. |
+
+## The seven principles
+
+1. **Proactive, not reactive** — A CI-friendly audit (`pnpm test`) blocks
+   unapproved third parties, inline code, GET-based personal-data forms, and
+   CSP drift *before* deployment.
+2. **Privacy as the default** — Every optional consent category starts
+   `false`. Global Privacy Control / Do Not Track lock analytics and marketing
+   off and override earlier opt-ins. No banner is shown because nothing
+   optional runs; choices are available from the footer.
+3. **Embedded into design** — The CSP is generated from the vendor registry,
+   so a new third party cannot load without a reviewed registry entry.
+   Optional features must start through `DailyGrindPrivacy.onConsent()`.
+4. **Full functionality** — The site works without JavaScript, and with
+   images, storage, or cookies blocked. The hero falls back to a brand colour.
+5. **End-to-end security** — Strict CSP with Trusted Types, HSTS (production),
+   COOP/CORP, `nosniff`, `frame-ancestors 'none'`, a restrictive
+   `Permissions-Policy`, `private, no-cache` for pages, and logout via POST.
+6. **Visibility and transparency** — This document, the vendor registry, a
+   plain-language footer statement, a visible GPC confirmation, and
+   `/.well-known/gpc.json`.
+7. **Respect for the user** — One-click "Reject all", choices that are as easy
+   to withdraw as to give, and `DailyGrindPrivacy.reset()` to erase the record
+   on the device.
+
+## Security headers
+
+Set by `server.mjs` through `privacy/security-headers.mjs`:
+
+| Header | Value / purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Content-Security-Policy` | `default-src 'none'`; first-party scripts and styles only; images from `'self'` and approved vendors; `form-action 'self'`; `frame-ancestors 'none'`; `require-trusted-types-for 'script'`; `upgrade-insecure-requests` in production. |
+| `Referrer-Policy` | `same-origin`: other origins never receive page URLs. |
+| `Permissions-Policy` | Disables camera, mic, geolocation, payment, sensors, Topics/FLoC, FLEDGE, Attribution Reporting, Private State Tokens, and more. |
+| `Strict-Transport-Security` | 2 years, `includeSubDomains; preload` (production only). |
+| `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` / `-Resource-Policy` | `same-origin` (CORP is `cross-origin` for `.well-known` JSON/TXT). |
+| `X-Content-Type-Options` | `nosniff` |
+| `X-Frame-Options` | `DENY` (legacy clickjacking protection) |
+| `Cache-Control` | `private, no-cache` for HTML (pages show signed-in navigation). |
+| `X-DNS-Prefetch-Control` | `off` |
+| `Origin-Agent-Cluster` | `?1` |
+
+The page also contains a `<meta>` copy of the CSP and referrer policy for
+hosts that cannot set headers. The audit fails if the copy drifts.
+
+Geolocation is disabled. If the Locations page later needs "find nearest
+store", enable `geolocation=(self)` on that route only, request it from a user
+gesture, and keep the coordinates on the device.
+
+## Third-party audit (2026-11-22)
+
+| Origin | Purpose | Data exposed | Mitigations | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `https://images.unsplash.com` | Hero photo | IP, User-Agent | `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`, `crossorigin="anonymous"` (no cookies), image-only CSP scope | **Approved, temporary.** Self-host to remove. |
+| Google Fonts | — | IP on every view | System font stack | Rejected |
+| Analytics / ad pixels / session replay | — | Cross-site identifiers | — | Rejected |
+| Map / social embeds | — | Third-party cookies | `frame-src 'none'`; link out instead | Rejected |
+
+**Follow-up:** download the hero image to `public/assets/img/hero.jpg`,
+point the `<img>` at it, and delete the Unsplash entry from the registry.
+The CSP then becomes fully first-party. This was not done here because the
+build environment could not reach image CDNs.
+
+### Third-party review checklist
+
+Answer all of these before adding an entry to `privacy/third-parties.json`:
+
+- [ ] Is there a first-party or self-hosted alternative? If so, use it.
+- [ ] What personal data does the vendor receive (IP, identifiers, page URL, form data)?
+- [ ] Does it set cookies or use device storage? Is it a script, or an inert resource?
+- [ ] Is a data processing agreement in place? Where is the data stored or processed?
+- [ ] Which consent category gates it? Scripts must load only through `DailyGrindPrivacy.onConsent()`.
+- [ ] Use the narrowest CSP directive possible. Use `no-referrer` and `crossorigin="anonymous"` where you can.
+- [ ] Re-review every `reviewIntervalDays`. The audit warns when a review is overdue.
+
+## Backend requirements (outside this repository)
+
+- `POST /logout` must invalidate the session server-side and verify a CSRF
+  token or check `Origin`/`Sec-Fetch-Site`. Then return `Clear-Site-Data: "cache", "cookies", "storage"`.
+- Session cookies: `__Host-` prefix, `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`.
+- Honor the `Sec-GPC: 1` request header server-side as an opt-out of sale/share.
+- Truncate or anonymize IPs in access logs, and apply a short retention period.
